  "id": "mental-rehearsal",
  "term": "mental rehearsal",
  "definition": "Mental rehearsal is the process of practicing an action in the mind by holding its movement pattern in working memory without physically carrying it out. In this context, it refers to imagining the action itself as a way to prepare or prime later performance.",
